Package: reach.forcing
Title: Model Forcing from Checked Rain Gauge, Radar and Gridded Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Payne", email = "jonathan.payne@environment-agency.gov.uk",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Turns checked hydrometric and meteorological data into the forcing that
    rainfall-runoff models are driven by. Rebuilds catchment rainfall exactly as the
    operational forecasting system makes it (fixed Thiessen weights scaled up when gauges
    fail, a radar fallback, and a switch to radar below a temperature threshold), computes
    Thiessen weights from gauge locations and catchment boundaries, and measures each gauge
    against long-term references. Part of the reach.* family: data arrive through reach.io
    and are checked by reach.validate; reach.forcing fetches nothing itself.
